<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Appendix A: Detailed Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Geometry-Aware Triggers in the Poincaré Ball). ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall that <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{x}=2/(1-\|x\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{x}=2/(1-\|x\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the conformal factor and write <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> for the hyperbolic distance. For <math id="S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="S8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\|x\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\|x\|</annotation></semantics></math> and the outward radial unit vector <math id="S8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{x}=\coloneqq x/\|x\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{x}=\coloneqq x/\|x\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We collect two standard facts about radial geodesics in the Poincaré ball.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Radial geodesics and arclength)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Euclidean radius of the outward radial unit-speed geodesic <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> at hyperbolic arclength <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(0)=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(0)=r</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dr}{ds}=\frac{1-r^{2}}{2},\qquad s=\int_{r}^{r(s)}\frac{2}{1-\rho^{2}}\,d\rho=\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r(s)}{1-r(s)}\right)-\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r}{1-r}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dr}{ds}=\frac{1-r^{2}}{2},\qquad s=\int_{r}^{r(s)}\frac{2}{1-\rho^{2}}\,d\rho=\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r(s)}{1-r(s)}\right)-\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r}{1-r}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">so in particular</span></p>
<table id="S8.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s)=\tanh\!\Big(\operatorname{artanh}(r)+\frac{s}{2}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.896em;" width="1.896em"><mi>tanh</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>artanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s)=\tanh\!\Big(\operatorname{artanh}(r)+\frac{s}{2}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Along a radial curve the metric reduces to <math id="S8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ds=\lambda(r)\,dr=\frac{2}{1-r^{2}}dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ds=\lambda(r)\,dr=\frac{2}{1-r^{2}}dr</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields the ODE and primitive directly.
Solving for <math id="S8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s)</annotation></semantics></math> gives the stated formula.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Euclidean displacement under an outward radial step)<span id="Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With notation as above, the Euclidean displacement <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(x,s)=r(s)-r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(x,s)=r(s)-r</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S8.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(x,s)=\frac{(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)}{1+r\,\tanh(s/2)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(x,s)=\frac{(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)}{1+r\,\tanh(s/2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(x,s)\leq(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)\leq s/\lambda_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(x,s)\leq(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)\leq s/\lambda_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the formula for <math id="S8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s)</annotation></semantics></math> from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3 (Radial geodesics and arclength). ‣ 8 Appendix A: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and the identity
<math id="S8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(a+b)=\dfrac{\tanh a+\tanh b}{1+\tanh a\,\tanh b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(a+b)=\dfrac{\tanh a+\tanh b}{1+\tanh a\,\tanh b}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(\operatorname{artanh}r)=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>artanh</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(\operatorname{artanh}r)=r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(s/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(s/2)</annotation></semantics></math> as given, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s)=\frac{r+\tanh(s/2)}{1+r\,\tanh(s/2)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s)=\frac{r+\tanh(s/2)}{1+r\,\tanh(s/2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting <math id="S8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> yields the formula for <math id="S8.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(x,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(x,s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(s/2)\leq s/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(s/2)\leq s/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+r\,\tanh(s/2)\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+r\,\tanh(s/2)\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(x,s)\leq(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)\leq(1-r^{2})\frac{s}{2}=\frac{s}{\lambda_{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(x,s)\leq(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)\leq(1-r^{2})\frac{s}{2}=\frac{s}{\lambda_{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Geometry-Aware Triggers in the Poincaré Ball). ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i)</em><span id="S8.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> The exact formula for <math id="S8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(x,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(x,s)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma 4 (Euclidean displacement under an outward radial step). ‣ 8 Appendix A: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, with the bounds in its last line.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii)</em>
If <math id="S8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in the Euclidean metric, then</p>
<table id="S8.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq L_{E}\,\|\tau_{s}(x)-x\|_{2}=L_{E}\,\kappa(x,s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq L_{E}\,\|\tau_{s}(x)-x\|_{2}=L_{E}\,\kappa(x,s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Applying the bounds from part (i), we get
<math id="S8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq L_{E}(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq L_{E}(1-r^{2})\tanh(s/2)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S8.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-r^{2}=(1-r)(1+r)\leq 2(1-r)\leq 2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-r^{2}=(1-r)(1+r)\leq 2(1-r)\leq 2\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields</p>
<table id="S8.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\|x\|\geq 1-\delta}|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq 2L_{E}\delta\tanh(s/2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\|x\|\geq 1-\delta}|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq 2L_{E}\delta\tanh(s/2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.3" class="ltx_p">The expectation bound follows immediately.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(iii)</em>
Let <math id="S8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=x+\kappa u_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=x+\kappa u_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\in(0,1-r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\in(0,1-r)</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S8.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}=\|y\|=r+\kappa&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}=\|y\|=r+\kappa&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and the segment remains inside <math id="S8.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The hyperbolic distance between two points on the same radial geodesic equals the radial arclength:</p>
<table id="S8.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}(x,y)=\int_{r}^{r^{\prime}}\frac{2}{1-\rho^{2}}\,d\rho=\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r^{\prime}}{1-r^{\prime}}\right)-\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r}{1-r}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}(x,y)=\int_{r}^{r^{\prime}}\frac{2}{1-\rho^{2}}\,d\rho=\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r^{\prime}}{1-r^{\prime}}\right)-\ln\!\left(\frac{1+r}{1-r}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Substitute <math id="S8.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}=r+\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}=r+\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and rearrange to get</p>
<table id="S8.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}(x,y)=\ln\!\left(\frac{1-r}{1-r-\kappa}\right)+\ln\!\left(1+\frac{\kappa}{1+r}\right)\ \geq\ \ln\!\left(\frac{1-r}{1-r-\kappa}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}(x,y)=\ln\!\left(\frac{1-r}{1-r-\kappa}\right)+\ln\!\left(1+\frac{\kappa}{1+r}\right)\ \geq\ \ln\!\left(\frac{1-r}{1-r-\kappa}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Finally, with <math id="S8.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\delta(x)=1-r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\delta(x)=1-r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality <math id="S8.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\ln(1-t)\geq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\ln(1-t)\geq t</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S8.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="S8.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln\!\left(\frac{\delta}{\delta-\kappa}\right)=-\ln\!\left(1-\frac{\kappa}{\delta}\right)\ \geq\ \frac{\kappa}{\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi>ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln\!\left(\frac{\delta}{\delta-\kappa}\right)=-\ln\!\left(1-\frac{\kappa}{\delta}\right)\ \geq\ \frac{\kappa}{\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p7.4" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="S8.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}(x,y)\geq\kappa/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}(x,y)\geq\kappa/\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h4>

<div id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(1) The stealth guarantee depends <em id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">linearly</em> on the shell width <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and on <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(s/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(s/2)</annotation></semantics></math>; no appeal to “exponential” growth of the conformal factor is needed (indeed <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> grows rationally in <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\|x\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\|x\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>).
(2) Part (iii) formalizes amplification without coupling the Euclidean budget <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> beyond the natural feasibility condition <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math>; the per-unit amplification <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> scales like <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\delta</annotation></semantics></math> near the boundary.
(3) If a detector is Lipschitz in the <em id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hyperbolic</em> metric (say, <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D(y)-D(x)|\leq L_{g}\,d_{g}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D(y)-D(x)|\leq L_{g}\,d_{g}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>), then for the same trigger <math id="S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq L_{g}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D(\tau_{s}(x))-D(x)|\leq L_{g}s</annotation></semantics></math>; i.e., hyperbolic-aware detectors do not enjoy the vanishing bound, clarifying which regularity notion matters for stealth.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Appendix B: Detailed Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Defense-Utility Trade-off). ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Radial Defense)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A defense <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}:\mathbb{D}^{n}\to\mathbb{D}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}:\mathbb{D}^{n}\to\mathbb{D}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is radial if it preserves direction and moves points inward along radial geodesics with displacement depending only on the hyperbolic radial coordinate.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumption 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Recovery Success)<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The defense <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> successfully recovers an <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of triggered inputs.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumption 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Radial Sensitivity)<span id="Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The classifier <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> has radial sensitivity <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{g}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{g}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> along radial geodesics.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Radial-flow identity)<span id="Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\Phi_{s}(x))=\rho(x)+\tfrac{s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\Phi_{s}(x))=\rho(x)+\tfrac{s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}\bigl(x,\Phi_{s}(x)\bigr)=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}\bigl(x,\Phi_{s}(x)\bigr)=s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Along a radial geodesic one has <math id="S9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ds=\tfrac{2}{1-r^{2}}\,dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ds=\tfrac{2}{1-r^{2}}\,dr</annotation></semantics></math>, which integrates to
<math id="S9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\operatorname{artanh}(r(s))-2\operatorname{artanh}(r(0))=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>artanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>artanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\operatorname{artanh}(r(s))-2\operatorname{artanh}(r(0))=s</annotation></semantics></math>; hence <math id="S9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\Phi_{s}(x))=\rho(x)+s/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\Phi_{s}(x))=\rho(x)+s/2</annotation></semantics></math> and the geodesic arclength equals <math id="S9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Radiality reduces to a scalar profile)<span id="Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is radial in the sense of Definition <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Definition 5 (Radial Defense). ‣ 9 Appendix B: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, then for any <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(x)=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(x)=\rho</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S9.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}\bigl(\mathcal{M}(x),x\bigr)=\Delta(\rho)=2\bigl(\rho-m(\rho)\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}\bigl(\mathcal{M}(x),x\bigr)=\Delta(\rho)=2\bigl(\rho-m(\rho)\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which depends only on <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and not on the direction of <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition <math id="S9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves direction and maps <math id="S9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\rho)\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\rho)\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math> along the same radial geodesic.
Hence <math id="S9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{g}(\mathcal{M}(x),x)=2|\rho-m(\rho)|=2(\rho-m(\rho))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{g}(\mathcal{M}(x),x)=2|\rho-m(\rho)|=2(\rho-m(\rho))</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\rho)\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\rho)\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S9.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Defense-Utility Trade-off). ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim P</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\Phi_{s}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\Phi_{s}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8 (Radial-flow identity). ‣ 9 Appendix B: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <math id="S9.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(Z)=\rho(X)+\tfrac{s}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(Z)=\rho(X)+\tfrac{s}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Assumption <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Assumption 6 (Recovery Success). ‣ 9 Appendix B: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Lemma 9 (Radiality reduces to a scalar profile). ‣ 9 Appendix B: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="S9.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\Big[\,\Delta\bigl(\rho(X)+\tfrac{s}{2}\bigr)\ \geq\ \alpha s\,\Big]\ \geq\ \beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\Big[\,\Delta\bigl(\rho(X)+\tfrac{s}{2}\bigr)\ \geq\ \alpha s\,\Big]\ \geq\ \beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S9.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S9.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in <math id="S9.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S9.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\bigl(\rho(X)\bigr)\ \geq\ \Delta\bigl(\rho(X)+\tfrac{s}{2}\bigr)-L_{\Delta}\cdot\tfrac{s}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\bigl(\rho(X)\bigr)\ \geq\ \Delta\bigl(\rho(X)+\tfrac{s}{2}\bigr)-L_{\Delta}\cdot\tfrac{s}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore on the event in (<a href="#S9.E18" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 9 Appendix B: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) we have <math id="S9.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\rho(X))\geq\alpha s-\tfrac{L_{\Delta}}{2}s=\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\rho(X))\geq\alpha s-\tfrac{L_{\Delta}}{2}s=\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies</span></p>
<table id="S9.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\!\left[\,d_{g}\!\bigl(\mathcal{M}(X),X\bigr)=\Delta(\rho(X))\ \geq\ \alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s\,\right]\ \geq\ \beta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.441em;" width="0.441em"><mi>ℙ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\!\left[\,d_{g}\!\bigl(\mathcal{M}(X),X\bigr)=\Delta(\rho(X))\ \geq\ \alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s\,\right]\ \geq\ \beta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is the probability lower bound. Taking expectations and using nonnegativity gives:</span></p>
<table id="S9.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[d_{g}(\mathcal{M}(X),X)\bigr]\geq\mathbb{E}\bigl[\,\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s\cdot\mathbf{1}\{\Delta(\rho(X))\geq\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s\}\,\bigr]\geq\beta\,\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[d_{g}(\mathcal{M}(X),X)\bigr]\geq\mathbb{E}\bigl[\,\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s\cdot\mathbf{1}\{\Delta(\rho(X))\geq\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s\}\,\bigr]\geq\beta\,\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Next, by Assumption <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Assumption 7 (Radial Sensitivity). ‣ 9 Appendix B: Detailed Proof of Theorem ‣ Geometry-Aware Backdoor Attacks: Leveraging Curvature in Hyperbolic Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (applied with <math id="S9.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\mathcal{M}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\mathcal{M}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>), for each outcome</span></p>
<table id="S9.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|\ \geq\ \mu_{g}\,d_{g}\!\bigl(\mathcal{M}(X),X\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|\ \geq\ \mu_{g}\,d_{g}\!\bigl(\mathcal{M}(X),X\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations yields:</span></p>
<table id="S9.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|\right]\geq\mu_{g}\,\beta\,\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|\right]\geq\mu_{g}\,\beta\,\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, since at least a <math id="S9.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of the mass satisfies <math id="S9.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|\geq\mu_{g}\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|\geq\mu_{g}\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s</annotation></semantics></math> and the integrand is nonnegative elsewhere,</span></p>
<table id="S9.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S9.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|^{2}\right]\ \geq\ \beta\,(\mu_{g}\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|f_{\theta}(\mathcal{M}(X))-f_{\theta}(X)\|^{2}\right]\ \geq\ \beta\,(\mu_{g}\alpha_{\mathrm{eff}}s)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S9.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">which is the second moment bound.
∎</span></p>
